\subsection{One request at a time}

[[FBF.get_many]] sends its requests from several threads at once
(\cref{API}).
[[vcrpy]] cannot follow that: when requests overlap, it records only a few
of them and lets the others through unrecorded, and in replay it lets the
unrecorded ones go for the network.
The first real recording lost 153 of the 179 requests of one test that way,
and its replay then failed on the network block.
So a service test sends one request at a time: we set the number of
workers to one for every test marked [[vcr]].
[[get_many]] still runs its pool and returns the documents in order, so
only the overlap is not tested here; the hand-written fake in \cref{API}
tests that.
<<test fixtures>>=
@pytest.fixture(autouse=True)
def one_request_at_a_time(request, monkeypatch):
    """Let a service test send its requests one at a time, which is all
    that `vcrpy` can record."""
    if request.node.get_closest_marker("vcr") is not None:
        monkeypatch.setattr(fbf_api, "WORKERS", 1)
@

