The tests use a pseudonymizer of their own, not the one of the run, which
would note the made-up values as originals while recording and then look for
them in the real cassettes.
None of the personal values may survive, the secrets must become the
placeholder, and the title must stay as it is.
The user has only attributes that FBF's users have.
An [[avatar-url]] among them would by itself make the attributes look like a
person's, and the test would pass with the rule for [[users]] broken, so the
avatar sits in a resource of its own.
The email address is at a made-up university, not at a real domain.
It cannot be at [[example.com]] either: [[vcr_support]] keeps addresses at
