\subsubsection{Free text that is not a string}
\label{FreeTextObjects}

[[vcr_support]] replaces a free-text field only when its value is a string.
FBF's reflections are not: their [[body]] is a Quill Delta, the rich-text
format of FBF's editor,
\begin{center}
[[{"ops": [{"insert": "First line\n"}, {"insert": {"emoji": ...}}]}]]
\end{center}
so [[vcr_support]] walks into it, finds only the keys [[ops]] and
[[insert]], which name no free text, and records the prose as it is.
Nor does the scan after the run catch it, since prose has no shape that a
pattern could find.
We therefore replace a free-text field whose value is an object or a list
wholesale, and note its strings as originals, as [[vcr_support]] does for a
string.
A Delta becomes a Delta again, with the placeholder as its only text: the
drift comparison then still sees [[ops]] and [[insert]], and code that reads
the text of a Delta reads the placeholder.
Anything else becomes the placeholder, in a list if it was a list.

Relationships are the exception.
In JSON:API, [[comments]] and [[note]] are also names of relationships,
whose values are objects with [[data]] and [[links]]; those name resources
rather than hold text, and the client follows them, so the rule leaves the
[[relationships]] object alone.
The method that applies the rule, [[_free_text]], also decides which texts
are worth noting (\cref{FreeTextNoted}).
<<scrubbing for FBF>>=
def strings_in(value):
    """Yield the strings anywhere in `value`."""
    if isinstance(value, str):
        yield value
    elif isinstance(value, dict):
        for item in value.values():
            yield from strings_in(item)
    elif isinstance(value, list):
        for item in value:
            yield from strings_in(item)


def text_placeholder(value):
    """Return the placeholder for the free text held in `value`."""
    if isinstance(value, dict) and "ops" in value:
        return {"ops": [{"insert": vcr_support.FREE_TEXT_PLACEHOLDER}]}
    if isinstance(value, list):
        return [vcr_support.FREE_TEXT_PLACEHOLDER]
    return vcr_support.FREE_TEXT_PLACEHOLDER
@

