\subsubsection{Keywords}

A review criterion has [[aggregated-keywords]]: the words that FBF picks out
of the students' reviews, as an object keyed by the word.
Two things follow.
First, the keys of that object are student text, and any word can be one,
[[type]] and [[name]] included; the first recording failed on a keyword
[[type]] whose value was an object, which our test for a person's resource
tried to look up in a set.
A JSON:API resource has a string [[type]] and an [[id]], so we require both
before we take an object for a resource.
Second, the keywords are free text: they are words of the students' prose,
and a word can be a name.
So [[aggregated-keywords]] is a free-text key, and the object is replaced
wholesale like a Delta (\cref{FreeTextObjects}), keys and all.
<<scrubbing for FBF>>=
FBF_FREE_TEXT_KEYS |= {"aggregated-keywords"}
@

