\subsubsection{Scrubbing what is already scrubbed}

The pseudonymizer sees recorded responses a second time: [[vcrpy]] runs the
response hook also on the responses it loads from a cassette, which a
recording with [[--record-mode=once]] does for every cassette that already
exists.
The values are then our own placeholders and pseudonyms, and the
pseudonymizer took them for originals: it noted the placeholder for free
text in the list of originals, and the scan after the run found it, rightly, in
every cassette with free text.
A pseudonym fared worse: [[Person-]]\ldots\ became another pseudonym, and the
first one was noted as an original that the cassette is full of.

So scrubbing must leave its own output alone.
A name or a login that already is a pseudonym stays as it is (an email
address at [[example.invalid]], which ours are, [[vcr_support]] already
keeps), and neither placeholders nor pseudonyms are ever noted as
originals.
<<scrubbing for FBF>>=
OUR_PLACEHOLDERS = {vcr_support.FREE_TEXT_PLACEHOLDER,
                    vcr_support.CONTACT_PLACEHOLDER,
                    vcr_support.SECRET_PLACEHOLDER,
                    vcr_support.URL_PLACEHOLDER}
OUR_PSEUDONYM = re.compile(
    r"(?i)(?:person|user)-[0-9a-f]{6}(?:@example\.invalid)?")


def is_ours(value):
    """True if `value` is a placeholder or a pseudonym of ours."""
    return value in OUR_PLACEHOLDERS or bool(OUR_PSEUDONYM.fullmatch(value))
<<[[FBFPseudonymizer]] methods>>=
def _log(self, *values):
    super()._log(*[value for value in values if not is_ours(value)])


def name(self, value):
    return value if is_ours(value) else super().name(value)


def login(self, value):
    return value if is_ours(value) else super().login(value)
@

Let's verify it by scrubbing a document twice, while noting originals in a
file of our own: the second pass must change nothing and note nothing.
<<test functions>>=
SCRUBBED_TWICE = {"data": [
  {"type": "users", "id": "u1",
   "attributes": {"name": "Anna Andersson", "email": "anna@uni.example.se",
                  "login_id": "anna"}},
  {"type": "reflections", "id": "r1",
   "attributes": {"body": {"ops": [{"insert": "Ask Bo Berg.\n"}]},
